1) On trying to load the flask app page using alb dns name, it doesnt load

troubleshooting :

# 1. Check if tasks are healthy
aws ecs describe-services --cluster python-flask-cluster --services flask-service --region us-west-2 \
  --query "services[].{Status:status,Running:runningCount,Desired:desiredCount}" --output json

# 2. Check target group health
aws elbv2 describe-target-health --region us-west-2 \
  --target-group-arn $(aws elbv2 describe-target-groups --region us-west-2 --names flask-tg-blue --query "TargetGroups[0].TargetGroupArn" --output text)

Saw - 504 Gateway Time-out, Targets are unhealthy, ALB can't reach the containers on port 8080.

# 3. Test from EC2
curl -k https://flask-app-alb-350405504.us-west-2.elb.amazonaws.com

ALB 504 Gateway Timeout — Root Cause & Fix
Problem
Application deployed on ECS Fargate, containers running and healthy, but ALB returned 504 Gateway Time-out when accessed in the browser.

How We Troubleshot
Step 1: Checked ECS Service Status

aws ecs describe-services --cluster python-flask-cluster --services flask-service --region us-west-2 \
  --query "services[].{Status:status,Running:runningCount,Desired:desiredCount}" --output json
Result: Service active, tasks running ✅

Step 2: Checked Target Group Health

aws elbv2 describe-target-health --region us-west-2 --target-group-arn <tg-arn>
Result: Targets showing unhealthy with Target.Timeout

Step 3: Verified Containers Directly from EC2

curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" http://172.31.25.232:8080/health
Result: 200 — containers respond fine when accessed directly ✅

Step 4: Checked Security Groups
ALB SG outbound → All traffic ✅
ECS Task SG inbound → Port 8080 from ALB SG ✅
ECS Task SG outbound → All traffic ✅
Step 5: Checked Target Group Configuration

aws elbv2 describe-target-groups --region us-west-2 --names flask-tg-blue \
  --query "TargetGroups[].{HealthCheckProtocol:HealthCheckProtocol,Protocol:Protocol,Port:Port}"
Result:


{
    "HealthCheckProtocol": "HTTPS",
    "Protocol": "HTTPS",
    "Port": 443
}
Found the root cause!

Root Cause
The target group flask-tg-blue was created with:

Protocol: HTTPS
Port: 443
But the container only serves:

Protocol: HTTP
Port: 8080
The ALB was trying to forward traffic via HTTPS to a container that only understands HTTP. The container couldn't respond to the HTTPS handshake → timeout → 504.

How We Fixed It
Step 1: Changed Health Check to HTTP (Partial Fix)

aws elbv2 modify-target-group --region us-west-2 \
  --target-group-arn <tg-arn> \
  --health-check-protocol HTTP \
  --health-check-path /health \
  --health-check-port 8080
Result: Targets became "healthy" (health checks worked) but ALB still returned 504 because the forwarding protocol was still HTTPS.

Step 2: Created New Target Group with HTTP:8080

aws elbv2 create-target-group --region us-west-2 \
  --name flask-tg-blue-http \
  --protocol HTTP \
  --port 8080 \
  --vpc-id vpc-0d005c51180164271 \
  --target-type ip \
  --health-check-protocol HTTP \
  --health-check-path /health \
  --health-check-port 8080
Step 3: Updated HTTPS:443 Listener to Forward to New Target Group

LISTENER_ARN=$(aws elbv2 describe-listeners --region us-west-2 \
  --load-balancer-arn <alb-arn> \
  --query "Listeners[?Port==\`443\`].ListenerArn" --output text)

aws elbv2 modify-listener --region us-west-2 \
  --listener-arn $LISTENER_ARN \
  --default-actions Type=forward,TargetGroupArn=<new-http-tg-arn>
Step 4: Registered Task IPs in New Target Group

aws elbv2 register-targets --region us-west-2 \
  --target-group-arn <new-http-tg-arn> \
  --targets Id=172.31.45.246,Port=8080 Id=172.31.24.155,Port=8080
Result: Application Accessible ✅

ISSUE 2 :
Pipeline build stage failure :

Failure 1: Deploy Stage — Image Definitions File Not Found
Error:


Did not find the image definition file imagedefinations.json in the input artifacts ZIP file
Cause: Typo in the pipeline configuration — imagedefinations.json instead of imagedefinitions.json

Fix: Edited the Deploy stage in CodePipeline → Changed filename to imagedefinitions.json (correct spelling)

Failure 2: Deploy Stage — Target Group Not Associated with Load Balancer
Error:


The target group with targetGroupArn arn:aws:elasticloadbalancing:us-west-2:307946644949:targetgroup/flask-tg-blue/7675b66ad15ff8c4 does not have an associated load balancer
Cause: The ECS service was still using the old flask-tg-blue (HTTPS:443 protocol) target group, but we had switched the ALB listener to the new flask-tg-blue-http (HTTP:8080) target group. The old TG was no longer attached to any listener.

Fix:

Deleted the old ECS service
Deleted the stuck CloudFormation stack:

aws cloudformation delete-stack --stack-name ECS-Console-V2-Service-flask-service-python-flask-cluster-a6ad372b --region us-west-2
Recreated the ECS service pointing to flask-tg-blue-http
Re-ran the pipeline → Deploy succeeded ✅
